key":"xX3VgYVM4F"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":117,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next box shows how to set up a plot of a 5 degree isotherm in\nunskewed coordinates.   Note that I invert the yaxis so pressure increases\ndownwards, and I make y a log scale and draw a horizontal grid.","position":{"start":{"line":117,"column":1},"end":{"line":117,"column":1}},"key":"Cy9p4pyYA6"}],"key":"hiAatcHo0d"}],"key":"WHIpjrFMaE"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"press=np.linspace(200,1000,30)\ntemps=np.ones_like(press)*5\nfig,ax = plt.subplots(1,1,figsize=(10,8))\nax.plot(temps,press)\nax.set(xlim=[0,35])\nax.invert_yaxis()\nax.yaxis.grid(True)","key":"qye1ZhTtch"},{"type":"outputs","id":"RrsShYmD1w-G-HIyjPuw_","children":[],"key":"X6oSu2JxQk"}],"key":"ADJMmPkv9E"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":131,"column":1},"end":{"line":131,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Calculating skewed temperature coordinates","position":{"start":{"line":131,"column":1},"end":{"line":131,"column":1}},"key":"rC4RrscY7K"}],"identifier":"id-2-calculating-skewed-temperature-coordinates","label":"2. Calculating skewed temperature coordinates","html_id":"id-2-calculating-skewed-temperature-coordinates","implicit":true,"key":"rVMVUe1qWk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":133,"column":1},"end":{"line":137,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you try plotting your soundings on the conventional plot above, you’ll see\nthat the height-temperature dependence makes it difficult to see the temperature\nand dewpoint together.  The traditional approach is to slant the temperature\nline by a constant slope (note that this is different from rotating the line,\nbecause the y axis doesn’t change)","position":{"start":{"line":133,"column":1},"end":{"line":133,"column":1}},"key":"bTG7KZSGha"}],"key":"ExSuoO9hyZ"}],"key":"QkrbnPs44w"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"#listing for a405.skewT.skewlib.convertSkewToTemp\ndef convertSkewToTemp(xcoord, press, skew):\n    \"\"\"\n    convertSkewToTemp(xcoord, press, skew)\n\n    Determines temperature from knowledge of a plotting coordinate\n    system and corresponding plot skew.\n    \n    Parameters\n    - - - - - -\n    xcoord : int\n        X coordinate in temperature plotting coordinates.\n    press : float\n        Pressure (hPa).\n    skew : int\n        Skew of a given coordinate system.\n\n    Returns\n    - - - -\n    Temp : float\n        Converted temperature in degC.\n\n    Examples\n    - - - - -\n    >>> convertSkewToTemp(300, 8.e4, 30)\n    638.6934574096806\n    \n    \"\"\"\n    Temp = xcoord  + skew * np.log(press);\n    return Temp\n\n#listing for a405.skewT.skewlib.convertTempToSkew\ndef convertTempToSkew(Temp, press, skew):\n    \"\"\"\n    convertTempToSkew(Temp, press, skew)\n\n    Determines the transformed temperature in plotting coordinates.\n    \n    Parameters\n    - - - - - -\n    Temp : float\n        Temperature (degC)\n    press : float\n        Pressure (hPa).\n    skew : int\n        Designated skew factor of temperature.\n\n    Returns\n    - - - -\n    tempOut : float\n        Converted temperature (degC).\n\n    Examples\n    - - - - -\n    >>> convertTempToSkew(30., 8.e4, 30)\n    -308.69345740968055\n    \n    \"\"\"\n    \n    tempOut = Temp - skew * np.log(press);\n    return tempOut","key":"FERRW1IhEJ"},{"type":"outputs","id":"kxxf12OW1YQjttJ3uih6W","children":[],"key":"PheCkuGOB0"}],"key":"niM3uTesWd"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":203,"column":1},"end":{"line":203,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Determining the skew","position":{"start":{"line":203,"column":1},"end":{"line":203,"column":1}},"key":"wwHbqdqrnt"}],"identifier":"id-3-determining-the-skew","label":"3. Determining the skew","html_id":"id-3-determining-the-skew","implicit":true,"key":"M71v0RWFUu"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":205,"column":1},"end":{"line":210,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting a isotherm with a 45 degree slope in these coordinates is tricky, because it depends on\nthe shape of the plot and the exact range values chosen for the temperature and pressure axis.\nCalculating the slope that will give a 45 degree angle isn’t particularly hard (try it), but\nit’s easier to just try some different skew values, and then save the result so you can put\nyour data up in the same coordinates.  For square plots with typical sounding ranges setting\nskew = 30 Kelvin  is about right.  Below I show what 4 different values of the skew look like.","position":{"start":{"line":205,"column":1},"end":{"line":205,"column":1}},"key":"ySeUzzGb58"}],"key":"QH1hXhnoOn"}],"key":"vwAovuBKio"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"fig,axes = plt.subplots(2,2,figsize=(10,10))\naxes=axes.ravel()  #axes comes back as a 2x2 array, flatten it\npress=np.linspace(200,1000,30)\nthe_temp=5.\nlinelist=[]\nskew_vals=[10,20,30, 40]\nfor ax,skew in zip(axes,skew_vals):\n    xcoord=convertTempToSkew(the_temp,press,skew)\n    ax.plot(xcoord,press,label=skew)\n    ax.invert_yaxis()\n    ax.set_yscale('log')\n    locs = np.array(range(100, 1100, 100))\n    labels = locs\n    ax.yaxis.grid(True)\n    out=ax.legend()\n    TempTickLabels = range(-15, 40, 5)\n    TempTickCoords = TempTickLabels\n    skewTickCoords = convertTempToSkew(TempTickCoords, 1.e3, skew)\n    #ax.set_xticks(skewTickCoords)\n    #out=ax.set_xticklabels(TempTickLabels)\n    skewLimits = convertTempToSkew([5, 35], 1.e3, skew)\n    out=ax.set(xlim=skewLimits)","key":"OB30clL91i"},{"type":"outputs","id":"DGXtRupObqhvMhg-dZiBg","children":[],"key":"JWS1JnPj5I"}],"key":"pZAg5sfcWW"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":237,"column":1},"end":{"line":237,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. using makeSkewDry","position":{"start":{"line":237,"column":1},"end":{"line":237,"column":1}},"key":"B9ues9tw0h"}],"identifier":"id-4-using-makeskewdry","label":"4. using makeSkewDry","html_id":"id-4-using-makeskewdry","implicit":true,"key":"WCeZKlioqh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":239,"column":1},"end":{"line":239,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s a function that adds two contour grids in skewT coordinates","position":{"start":{"line":239,"column":1},"end":{"line":239,"column":1}},"key":"bWBmvgKm6A"}],"key":"SxmH6DKwWV"}],"key":"BwtdsqCJyM"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from cloudlib.skewT.skewlib import makeSkewDry\nhelp(makeSkewDry)","key":"u5lgoDORCQ"},{"type":"outputs","id":"JalwPGrwqaq6yAT1hN1Zz","children":[],"key":"SxV9MbICcX"}],"key":"VBto6i6Nme"},{"type":"block","children":[],"key":"pN32rea2Ou"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"fig,ax =plt.subplots(1,1,figsize=(8,8))\nax,skew = makeSkewDry(ax)","key":"cgYPp0VydR"},{"type":"outputs","id":"MHVCt0yz19cfaM3HGWlaC","children":[],"key":"xbYmBffEga"}],"key":"N6Pv2zXI1A"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":251,"column":1},"end":{"line":251,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 Adding information to the plot","position":{"start":{"line":251,"column":1},"end":{"line":251,"column":1}},"key":"YURUlEv2Op"}],"identifier":"id-5-adding-information-to-the-plot","label":"5 Adding information to the plot","html_id":"id-5-adding-information-to-the-plot","implicit":true,"key":"jcO7NJO9yL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":253,"column":1},"end":{"line":253,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"use the display finction to redraw the axis after you modify it","position":{"start":{"line":253,"column":1},"end":{"line":253,"column":1}},"key":"wLBxRHcj98"}],"key":"LaFyeJtXbC"}],"key":"MfA3tIohIW"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"ax.set(title='new title')\ndisplay(fig)","key":"cKsQw3Udol"},{"type":"outputs","id":"xBhyrZeH-wLlgz7mfq0a7","children":[],"key":"sr0XIchJCg"}],"key":"JuJi79t6Qx"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":260,"column":1},"end":{"line":260,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Add a datapoint to the skewT diagram","position":{"start":{"line":260,"column":1},"end":{"line":260,"column":1}},"key":"IvnkLAePSo"}],"identifier":"id-6-add-a-datapoint-to-the-skewt-diagram","label":"6. Add a datapoint to the skewT diagram","html_id":"id-6-add-a-datapoint-to-the-skewt-diagram","implicit":true,"key":"y0nHkdofnW"}],"key":"brIWw9Upx5"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"temp=-10\npress=600\nskewtemp=convertTempToSkew(temp,press,skew)\nax.plot(skewtemp,press,'ro',markersize=30)\ndisplay(fig)","key":"HPsuwWGZGr"},{"type":"outputs","id":"UBYc1qliz0CHaai32p_2M","children":[],"key":"dbQOVguEez"}],"key":"s6dBNAhhto"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":270,"column":1},"end":{"line":270,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"7 change the axes","position":{"start":{"line":270,"column":1},"end":{"line":270,"column":1}},"key":"ggJitXayKU"}],"identifier":"id-7-change-the-axes","label":"7 change the axes","html_id":"id-7-change-the-axes","implicit":true,"key":"qxkk1RJML1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":272,"column":1},"end":{"line":273,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s how to change the xaxis so that the left corner at 1000 hPa goes down to -35 deg C\nand the upper boundary stops at 600 hPa","position":{"start":{"line":272,"column":1},"end":{"line":272,"column":1}},"key":"UbEAQk0BVh"}],"key":"jxkmgnfxLA"}],"key":"v3iHAwESui"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"skewLimits = convertTempToSkew([-35, 35], 1.e3, skew)\nout=ax.set(xlim=skewLimits,ylim=(1000.,600.))\ndisplay(fig)","key":"SQrcjokmwl"},{"type":"outputs","id":"489hBcQlzzSYQkoDpnYpW","children":[],"key":"E6v7O1qtMI"}],"key":"dGsHUdqcBd"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":281,"column":1},"end":{"line":281,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full example","position":{"start":{"line":281,"column":1},"end":{"line":281,"column":1}},"key":"UUXhGeOJsy"}],"identifier":"full-example","label":"Full example","html_id":"full-example","implicit":true,"key":"Ta4QHpAoEK"}],"key":"yMLRC6mSuY"},{"type":"block","position":{"start":{"line":283,"column":1},"end":{"line":283,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":285,"column":1},"end":{"line":285,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In cells below, we add the temperature and dewpoint soundings for the Feb 1, 2013 brazil sounding to this plot","position":{"start":{"line":285,"column":1},"end":{"line":285,"column":1}},"key":"EYG4AU2ObE"}],"key":"yG8YfHaswP"}],"key":"Lg4AGH8nRI"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"press,temp = the_sound['pres'].to_numpy(), the_sound['temp'].to_numpy()\ndewpoint= the_sound['dwpt'].to_numpy(copy=True)","key":"xVeOgr7QIP"},{"type":"outputs","id":"OkcF4uF5dzvp_2UQ8FPXK","children":[],"key":"Iea1s0brl4"}],"key":"SbDjYIJwUB"},{"type":"block","children":[],"key":"x5MwhDDzxh"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"hit = dewpoint < -10\ndewpoint[hit] = np.nan","key":"Ueo3ukc3a8"},{"type":"outputs","id":"gnhu613kE1IgMe6FMpjF7","children":[],"key":"LTN4DKNVLC"}],"key":"b1N8GOBSjW"},{"type":"block","children":[],"key":"ASe3tYcuf4"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"skew=30\nskewtemp=convertTempToSkew(temp,press,skew)\nskewdewpoint = convertTempToSkew(dewpoint,press,skew)\nfig,ax =plt.subplots(1,1,figsize=(8,8))\nax,skew = makeSkewDry(ax,skew=skew)\nax.plot(skewtemp,press,'r-')\nax.plot(skewdewpoint,press,'g-')\nskewLimits = convertTempToSkew([15, 25], 1.e3, skew)\nout=ax.set(xlim=skewLimits,ylim=(1000.,400.))","key":"kDuOfc7OUL"},{"type":"outputs","id":"28VKi7-xTrZ18WgEILqbw","children":[],"key":"EUFCODBKFm"}],"key":"NpCn4YMiqz"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":309,"column":1},"end":{"line":309,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using the metpy skewT library","position":{"start":{"line":309,"column":1},"end":{"line":309,"column":1}},"key":"ju0dJyF5JY"}],"identifier":"using-the-metpy-skewt-library","label":"Using the metpy skewT library","html_id":"using-the-metpy-skewt-library","implicit":true,"key":"pA6OMmvXA8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":311,"column":1},"end":{"line":311,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repeat this using the ","position":{"start":{"line":311,"column":1},"end":{"line":311,"column":1}},"key":"Ifz7KLF3Nw"},{"type":"link","url":"https://unidata.github.io/MetPy/latest/examples/plots/Simple_Sounding.html#sphx-glr-examples-plots-simple-sounding-py","position":{"start":{"line":311,"column":1},"end":{"line":311,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"metpy skewT library","position":{"start":{"line":311,"column":1},"end":{"line":311,"column":1}},"key":"jG5TMXbhol"}],"urlSource":"https://unidata.github.io/MetPy/latest/examples/plots/Simple_Sounding.html#sphx-glr-examples-plots-simple-sounding-py","key":"xMyXKIqcoH"}],"key":"kQ7pjn6iCN"}],"key":"yBKyEwfIZU"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from metpy.plots import SkewT\nfrom metpy.units import units\nfig,ax =plt.subplots(1,1,figsize=(8,8))\nfig.clf()\nskew_plot = SkewT(fig)\nskew_plot.ax.set_title(\"metpy example\")\nskew_plot.ax.set(xlim=(0,25),ylim=(1000,600))\ntheta = np.array([0,10,20,30,40,50,60]) + 273.15\ntheta = theta*units(\"K\")\nskew_plot.plot_dry_adiabats(t0=theta)\nskew_plot.plot_moist_adiabats()\nskew_plot.plot_mixing_lines()\nskew_plot.plot(press,temp,'r')\nskew_plot.plot(press,dewpoint,'g');","key":"nkCiDAfFnU"},{"type":"outputs","id":"UgM-ayK2gf5DDl3XRIx4x","children":[],"key":"kOoGkxZd9A"}],"key":"Dk2sTHjId5"},{"type":"block","children":[],"key":"sJ4Jjv8fnl"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"","key":"bLAsqg7YLF"},{"type":"outputs","id":"8Z_ERWgA7JaDlpVNbIV3L","children":[],"key":"V2OpG2fvLO"}],"key":"sugZzBN0TA"}],"key":"FjLVoz1qqc"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Worksheet2 -- Thermodynamics worksheet solution","url":"/notebooks/worksheets/worksheet2-solution","group":"Worksheets"},"next":{"title":"worksheet 3 solution: working with numpy arrays","url":"/notebooks/worksheets/worksheet3-derivs-and-ints-solution","group":"Worksheets"}}},"domain":"http://pre.render"}